  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Generative ensembles for proteins, antibodies, IDPs and RNA now sit alongside benchmarks showing cofolding gets ligands right while protein conformation lags.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread treats biomolecules as conformational distributions carrying energetic annotations rather than single static poses. OriDynamics targets all-atom ensembles across monomers and complexes with ligands or partners; Cadense generates antibody Fv ensembles from sequence trained against MD-derived distributions; the bAIes framework is extended across six predictors (AlphaFold2/3, Boltz-1/2, ESMFold, ESMFold2) for atomic-resolution IDP ensembles; REVEAL couples secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR; transition-conditioned dynamical fingerprints rank microscopic players inside rare-event transition corridors. Cross-state learning (AllositeUltra, AsBench2) extends this to apo versus substrate-bound allosteric sites. A second strand injects physics into learned representations: HEIWA adds explicit-implicit solvent attention to ESM3, StableProt fuses 3Di tokens with SaProt for Tm/OGT, and EvoPhi-DDG is antisymmetrized with JanusDDG. A cofolding benchmark across AlphaFold3, RoseTTAFold3, Boltz-2 and Chai-1 finds correct ligand placement decoupled from accurate protein conformation, motivating the shift.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-13"
}
